---
source: crates/cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "sb.ok(&[\"--help\"]).stdout"
---
Swarm Simulator, on the command line.

The save lives in $XDG_DATA_HOME/swarm/save.txt (default ~/.local/share/swarm/save.txt); override it with --save or $SWARM_SAVE. Each command that changes the game rewrites the save (v2) and keeps the previous one as save.prev.txt.

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 refused by a game rule, 2 usage error, 3 I/O error.

Usage: swarm [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  new           Start a new game
  show          Show units, upgrades and tabs
  buy           Buy units
  buy-max       Buy as many units as you can afford
  upgrade       Buy upgrade or ability levels
  upgrade-max   Buy as many levels of an upgrade as you can afford
  upgrade-all   Buy every affordable, watched upgrade (the game's "buy all upgrades")
  ascend        Ascend: trade energy for mutagen and start over
  respec        Respec mutations: uses a free respec if you have one, else energy
  undo          Undo the last command; run again to redo
  advance       Let game time pass: 90s, 3h, 2d, 1h30m
  export        Print the save
  import        Replace the game with a save from a file (v1 or v2; `-` is stdin)
  convert       Convert a save file between formats without touching your game
  scenario      Run and compare parity scenarios (swarm-scenario)
  bench         Time engine operations
  stats         Show statistics: time played, purchases
  achievements  Show achievements
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --save <PATH>
          The save file

      --long
          Long number names ("1.23456 million") instead of short ("1.23M")

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
